# Reference SGML that repeats a DECLARED-but-not-allowed element (zz, valid only
# nowhere inside doc's `(a)*` model) 250 times. Each occurrence is one
# elementNotAllowed error; onsgmls's ErrorCountEventHandler cancels the parse the
# instant the count reaches DEFAULT_ERROR_LIMIT (200): the content loop stops
# WITHOUT closing the open elements or emitting the conformance marker, so the
# ESIS is truncated at the 200th start tag (200 (ZZ, 199 )ZZ, 199 -x), and a
# final locationless Info line "maximum number of errors (200) reached; change
# with -E option" is printed. Exit 1.
BASE=entry
DOC=doc.sgm
